{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Hahn|mono-stratified|bistratified|bis-stratified|synaptic|intrinsically photosensitive retinal ganglion cell' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"4932:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D011689\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12907269\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14568361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31424738\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33288911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38168772\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000121 \"An inhibitory neuron and the sole output neuron of the cerebellar cortex, the Purkinje cell's soma is located between the granular and molecular layers of the cerebellum. It is one of the largest neural cells in the mammalian brain, ranging from 50 to 80 micrometres in diameter. Purkinje cells have planar, fan-shaped dendrites that branch extensively with little overlap. This cell type receives synaptic input from parallel fibres, which modulate high-frequency spike activity known as \\\"simple spikes,\\\" and climbing fibres, which modulate infrequent calcium spike activity known as \\\"complex spikes\\\". Purkinje cells are involved in motor coordination, particularly in correcting movements in progress.\")\n9337:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Bergmann_Glial_Cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000644 \"Type of radial astrocyte in the cerebellar cortex that have their cell bodies in the Purkinje cell layer and processes that extend into the molecular layer, terminating with bulbous endfeet at the pial surface. Bergmann glia express high densities of glutamate transporters that limit diffusion of the neurotransmitter glutamate during its release from synaptic terminals. Besides their role in early development of the cerebellum, Bergmann glia are also required for the pruning or addition of synapses.\")\n9429:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16687276\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinealocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000652 \"This cell type produces and secretes melatonin and forms the pineal parenchyma. Extending from each cell body, which has a spherical, oval or lobulated mucleus, are one or more tortuous basophilic processes, containing parallel microtubules known as synaptic ribbons. These processes end in expanded terminal buds near capillaries or less, frequently, ependymal cells of the pineal recess. The terminal buds contain granular endoplasmic reticulum, mitochondria and electron-dense cored vesicles, which store monoamines and polypeptide hormones, release of which appears to require sympathetic innervation.\")\n9734:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000688 \"A fibroblast-like cell that provides support at neuromuscular junctions in vertebrates and are localized outside the synaptic basal lamina.\")\n9762:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18803315\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000692 \"perisynaptic Schwann cell\")\n17052:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15738192\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002285 \"A taste receptor cell that is characterized by morphologically identifiable synaptic contacts with the gustatory nerve fibers and expression of the synaptic membrane protein-25 (SNAP-25) and NCAM.\")\n21005:# Class: obo:CL_0003001 (bistratified retinal ganglion cell)\n21013:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0003001 \"bistratified retinal ganglion cell\")\n21030:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003003 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a small dendritic field and a sparse dendritic arbor with post sympatic terminals in sublaminar layer S3.\")\n21043:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003004 \"A bistratified retinal ganglion cell that has a small dendritic field with sparse density that terminates at the intersection of the S4-S5 sublaminar level, and a second dendrite field that is medium in size and degree of arborization that terminates in sublaminar layer S2.\")\n21048:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0003004 \"is_a bistratified retinal ganglion cell S4-S5 dendrite field having (small dendritic field, sparse density) and second dendrite field having (medium, meduim)\")\n21059:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003005 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a small dendritic field and dense dendritic arbor.\")\n21099:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003008 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a medium dendritic field and a medium dendritic arbor with post sympatic terminals in sublaminar layer S2.\")\n21112:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003009 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a medium dendritic field and a sparse dendritic arbor with post sympatic terminals in sublaminar layer S4 and S5.\")\n21126:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003010 \"A bistratified retinal ganglion cell that has a dendrite field that terminates in sublaminar layer S2 and a second dendrite field that terminates in sublaminar layer S4.\")\n21141:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003011 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a large dendritic field and a sparse dendritic arbor with post synaptic terminals in sublaminar layer S4.\")\n21154:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003012 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a large dendritic field and a medium dendritic arbor with post synaptic terminals in sublaminar layer S1 and S2.\")\n21168:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003013 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a large dendritic field, a medium dendritic arbor, and a long secondary dendrite shaft with post synaptic terminals in sublaminar layer S4.\")\n21182:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003014 \"A mono-stratified retinal ganglion cell that has a large dendritic field, a medium dendritic arbor, and a medium length secondary dendrite shaft.\")\n21195:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003015 \"A G11 retinal ganglion cell that has post synaptic terminals in sublaminar layer S4 and is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n21207:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11978858\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003016 \"A G11 retinal ganglion cell that has post synaptic terminals in sublaminar layer S2 and is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21219:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003017 \"A retinal ganglion B cell that has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21242:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003020 \"A retinal ganglion cell C that has post-synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21305:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003026 \"A bistratified retinal ganglion cell that has a small dendrite fields with a sparse dendrite arbor terminating in S2 and S3.\")\n21319:AnnotationAssertion(Annot