 is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n21461:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003038 \"An M7 retinal ganglion cells with synaptic terminals in S2 and is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21497:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003041 \"An M9 retinal ganglion cells with synaptic terminals in S2 and is depolarized by illumination of its receptive field center.\")\n21509:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003042 \"An M9 retinal ganglion cell with synaptic terminals in S4 that is depolarized by decreased illumination of their receptive field center\")\n21533:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003044 \"A bistratified ganglion cell with small, dense dendritic fields that terminate in S1 and S3.\")\n21547:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16626866\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0003045 \"A bistratified ganglion cell with larger, asymetric dendritic fields that terminate in S2 and S4.\")\n21695:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004119 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has medium body size, medium dendritic field and dense dendritic arbor, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21724:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12209831\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004121 \"A retinal ganglion cell B that has a very small but very dense dendritic field, and has post synaptic terminals in S2.\")\n21866:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004215 \"A type 5 cone bipolar cell with narrowly stratified post synaptic terminals.\")\n21936:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24246263\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004221 \"A flag amacrine cell with post-synaptic terminals in S2 and S3. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n21949:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24246263\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004222 \"A flag amacrine cell with post-synaptic terminals in S3, S4, and S5. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n21963:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004223 \"A amacrine cell with a small dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S1, S2, S3, and S4. AB diffuse-1 amacrine cells have a tent-shaped dendritic arbor and undulate dendrites.\")\n21977:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004224 \"A broadly stratifying amacrine cell that has a small dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S2 and S3. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n21990:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004225 \"A broadly stratifying amacrine cell with a small dendritic field, straight dendrites and post-synaptic terminals in S1, S2, and S3.\")\n22003:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004226 \"An amacrine cell with a small dendritic field with post-synaptic terminals in S3 and S4.\")\n22013:# Class: obo:CL_0004227 (flat bistratified amacrine cell)\n22015:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25630271\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004227 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field. Flat bistratified amacrine cells have post-synaptic terminals both on the border of S1 and S2, and on the border of S3 and S4. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n22020:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004227 \"flat bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22029:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004228 \"An amacrine cell with a small dendritic field that has post-synaptic terminals in S1, S2, S3, and S4.\")\n22043:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004229 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field that has dendrite stratification in S2, and in S3 and S4.\")\n22054:# Class: obo:CL_0004230 (diffuse bistratified amacrine cell)\n22056:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004230 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a small dendritic field that has post-synaptic terminals in S1 and the border of S1-S2, and termination of a second arbor within the border of S2-S3 and S3.\")\n22061:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004230 \"diffuse bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22071:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004231 \"A broadly stratifying amacrine cell with a small dendritic field and a complex dendritic arbor. Recurving diffuse amacrine cells have post-synaptic terminals in S2, S3, and S4.\")\n22084:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004232 \"An amacrine cell with a flat dendritic arbor and a medium dendritic field. Starburst amacrine cells have post-synaptic terminals in S2. This cell type releases the neurotransmitters gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) and acetylcholine.\")\n22097:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9194315\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004233 \"An amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals that stratify at S2, with a second stratification that occurs in S3 and S4. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter glycine.\")\n22111:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004234 \"An amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S2, and in S3-S4.\")\n22123:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004235 \"An amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S2 and S3. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA).\")\n22136:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004236 \"An amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S2, S3, and S4. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA).\")\n22150:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10614594\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004237 \"A retinal amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S1, S2, S3, and S4. This cell type releases the neurotransmitter gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA).\")\n22163:# Class: obo:CL_0004238 (asymmetric bistratified amacrine cell)\n22165:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004238 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field, a flat and sparse dendritic arbor, and post-synaptic terminals at the intersections of S1 and S2, and S3 and S4.\")\n22170:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004238 \"asymmetric bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22176:# Class: obo:CL_0004239 (wavy bistratified amacrine cell)\n22178:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004239 \"A bistratified amacrine cell with a medium dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S1-S2, and S4.\")\n22183:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004239 \"wavy bistratified amacrine cell\")\n22192:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004240 \"An amacrine cell with a wide dendritic field, dendrites in S1, and post-synaptic terminals in S1.\")\n22203:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004241 \"An amacrine cell with a wide dendritic field, dendrites in S2, and post-synaptic terminals in S1.\")\n22214:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004242 \"An amacrine cell with a wide dendritic field, dendrites in S3, and post-synaptic terminals in S3. Dendrites of this cell type are straight and minimally branched.\")\n22225:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004243 \"An amacrine cell with a wild dendritic field, dendrites in S3, and post-synaptic terminals in S3. Dendrites have spikes, cross over each other, and cover a larger volume than dendrties of W3-1 retinal amacrine cells.\")\n22236:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004244 \"An amacrine cell with a wide dendritic field, dendrites in S4, and post-synaptic terminals in S4.\")\n22247:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12486181\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9620701\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0004245 \"An amacrine cell with a wide dendritic field and post-synaptic terminals in S5. This cell type releases the neurotransmitters gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) and serotonin.\")\n22268:# Class: obo:CL_0004247 (bistratified cell)\n22274:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004247 \"bistratified cell\")\n22278:# Class: obo:CL_0004250 (bistratified retinal amacrine cell)\n22285:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0004250 \"bistratified retinal amacrine cell\")\n22714:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1087183\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007017 \"An epidermal cell with apical microvilli or a single apical projection have synaptic associations with nerve fibres in the epidermis.\")\n24654:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18677503\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2273099\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011006 \"A cerebellar interneuron characterized by a spindle-shaped or triangular soma, parasagittally oriented and located at the border between the granular layer and the Purkinje cell layer. The Lugaro cell extends dendrites predominantly in the parasagittal plane, forming synaptic interactions with basket, stellate, and Golgi cells. Its axonal projections extend upward into the molecular layer, where they form a parasagittal plexus and emit long transverse collaterals that run parallel to the long axis of the cerebellar folia. The Lugaro cell is capable of co-releasing GABA and glycine, as evidenced by the expression of glutamate decarboxylase (GAD65/67) and the glycine transporter GlyT2.\")\n25460:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10377365\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25876458\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29651049\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37905876\") terms:description obo:CL_0020008 \"Although they constitute only 1–3% of all striatal neurons, these interneurons form a major modulatory hub, integrating cortical, thalamic, and dopaminergic inputs and shaping striatal output dynamics (Gonzales & Smith, 2015; Wegman et al., 2024). Electrophysiologically, the neuron exhibits tonic autonomous firing at 3–10 Hz, broad action potentials, and a prominent hyperpolarization-activated inward current (Ih) (Bennett & Wilson, 1999; Goldberg & Reynolds, 2011). Functionally, it modulates corticostriatal and thalamostriatal synaptic transmission, dopamine release, and spiny projection neuron excitability through co-transmission of acetylcholine and GABA (Lozovaya et al., 2018; Wegman et al., 2024). This dual inhibitory and modulatory signaling underlies context-dependent control of synaptic plasticity, action selection, and reinforcement learning (Gonzales & Smith, 2015; Lozovaya et al., 2018).\")\n25632:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000222 \"A specialised neuroendocrine cell located in the gastric mucosa that regulates digestive processes including acid secretion and gut motility. This cell stores hormones in large dense core vesicles and synaptic-like microvesicles.\")\n28368:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0009943\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001435 \"The small neuron in the glomerular layer of the olfactory bulb whose dendrites arborize within a glomerulus, where it receives synaptic input from olfactory receptor cell axon terminals, and also engages in dendrodendritic interactions with mitral and tufted cell dendrites; uses both GABA and dopamine as a neurotransmitter.\")\n29102:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32990595\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8915580\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000027 \"A GABAergic inhibitory interneuron located in the molecular layer of the cerebellar cortex. It projects axons that form specialized synaptic structures around Purkinje cells, including pericellular baskets, which wrap around the Purkinje cell soma, and the pinceau: a brush-like terminal that contacts the initial segment of the Purkinje cell axon. The basket cell modulates Purkinje cell activity through both chemical (GABAergic) and non-synaptic (ephaptic) mechanisms. It is arranged in sagittal rows that align with Purkinje cell zones, contributing to the cerebellum's modular and topographically organized architecture. It plays an essential role in regulating motor coordination and potentially cognitive functions.\")\n30133:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023024 \"A lamp5 GABAergic cortical interneuron with layer-adapting morphology. NGC lamp5 cells have a small round soma, short dendrites, and a wide dense axonal arbor that tends to establish a dense axonal mesh with high connection probability both to themselves and L2 pyramidal cells. NGC lamp5 cells have unique synaptic properties that distinguish them from other GABAergic interneurons, including the release of GABA to the extracellular space via volume transmission, and the ability to produce GABA-B responses in connected postsynaptic targets.\")\n30279:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15378039\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27199673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023036 \"A transcriptomically distinct pvalb GABAergic interneuron located in the pallium. It is recognizable by the straight terminal axonal 'cartridges' of vertically oriented strings of synaptic boutons. Chandelier PV cells' boutons target exclusively the axon initial segment (AIS) of pyramidal cells, with a single cell innervating hundreds of pyramidal cells in a clustered manner.  These cells are fast-spiking.\")\n31008:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25355208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023114 \"A vestibular afferent neuron which posseses a unique postsynaptic terminal, the calyx, which completely covers the basolateral walls of type I hair cells and receives input from multiple ribbon synapses.\")\n32295:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033019 \"The axons of a blue cone bipolar cell terminate close to the ganglion cell layer, where they transfer the S-cone ON signal to small bistratified ganglion cells. Other targets of a blue cone bipolar cell include amacrine cells and possibly large bistratified ganglion cells.\")\n32369:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22006647\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033027 \"An OFF diffuse bipolar cell that makes synaptic contact with both L/M and S-cone photoreceptors and only minimal contact with rod photoreceptors.\")\n32382:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25309346\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26500507\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033028 \"An OFF diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells. This cell contains a large number of synaptic ribbons and a small axon arbor area.\")\n32440:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033034 \"An ON bipolar cell with a small dendritic tree that forms most of the central (invaginating) elements opposite the synaptic ribbon at the cone triad.\")\n32453:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033035 \"A giant bipolar cell is usually monostratified, although, very rarely, it can be bistratified.\")\n32646:# Class: obo:CL_4033053 (small bistratified retinal ganglion cell)\n32651:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell\")\n32652:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1002/cne.22183\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell, blue-ON/yellow-OFF ganglion cell\")\n32656:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified retinal ganglion cell\")\n33184:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19279265\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25904839\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37139179\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042007 \"An astrocyte with highly branched protrusions, found in neocortex layers 2-6. It is involved with the formation and elimination of synapses, glutamate clearance, modulation of synaptic functions and regulation of blood flow in response to synaptic activity.\")\n33547:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30467465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042037 \"Some striatal SST GABAergic neurons can co-release glutamate and generate excitation-inhibition responses in postsynaptic neurons. This interneuron type has the least dense dendritic branches in the striatum. In the dorsomedial striatum these neurons regulate the activity of striatal projection neurons.\")\n33742:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-020-0271-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1038/s41575-021-00561-y\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32152479\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34170401\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4047038 \"A multipolar neuron in the myenteric plexus of the gastrointestinal tract, characterized by a small to medium-sized cell body and multiple short dendrites.  This neuron exhibits fast excitatory postsynaptic potentials and can be classified into stubby, spiny and hairy subtypes based on dendritic morphology. (Brehmer, 2021)\")\n34166:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33037211\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33311457\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33311464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052025 \"A specialized muscle nucleus that is part of an extrafusal muscle fiber, clustered at the postsynaptic side of the neuromuscular junction. This nucleus exhibits a distinct transcriptional profile, including acetylcholine receptor (AChR) subunit genes. It regulates the production of proteins essential for maintaining the structure and function of the neuromuscular junction, supporting efficient nerve-muscle signaling for muscle contraction.\")\n34860:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31982322\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39303139\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072018 \"A neuron that generates rhythmic bursts of action potentials independently of synaptic input. This intrinsic property enables it to maintain oscillatory activity even when isolated from other neurons. It populates the brainstem, hypothalamus, basal ganglia, spinal cord, and cerebellum. It plays a crucial role in regulating circadian rhythms in the suprachiasmatic nucleus, generating respiratory rhythms in the preBötzinger complex, and synchronizing neural networks.\")\n35319:# Class: obo:GO_0051932 (synaptic transmission, GABAergic)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing mouse RGC classes are already present, but they mostly lack the formal axioms the linked sub-issue describes. I’m checking whether there is a consistent, bounded pattern already in the file for `ON/OFF`, `bistratified`, and named parentage before deciding whether to patch that subset or treat the epic as still too underspecified."}}
